## 🚫 What NOT to Do

**Don't:** push to `master` (or to `develop` from a worktree) · open PRs to `master` outside a production release · commit without a descriptive message · open a PR without a proper description · merge your own PR without the gates passing · force-push shared branches · commit secrets · skip testing before a PR · ignore SwiftLint warnings · leave commented-out code · open massive PRs (>500 lines) · switch branches inside a worktree.

**Do:** branch from `develop` and target `develop` · run the worktree check at the start of every task · write clear commit messages and PR descriptions · wait for the gates before merging · test locally and run lint · keep PRs focused · update docs when needed · follow existing patterns · track multi-step work with the todo tool.

