## 👀 PR Review Workflow (Reviewer's Guide)

Use `gh-bot-review` (never `gh pr review`, which cannot approve same-account PRs). Always pass `--repo <owner>/<repo>`.

1. **Triage:** `gh pr view <N>`, `gh pr diff <N> --stat`. Check title format, description, size (<500 lines) and target (`develop`).
2. **Checkout:** `gh pr checkout <N>`.
3. **Checklist:** security (no secrets, no injection) · architecture (follows patterns, DRY) · quality (no force unwraps, proper error handling) · performance (`[weak self]`, no main-thread blocking) · testing (edge cases, error paths).
4. **Submit:** `gh-bot-review --pr <N> --repo <owner>/<repo> --event APPROVE|REQUEST_CHANGES --body "..."`. For a long review, write `/tmp/review-<N>.md` and pass `--body-file`.

**Approve when:** CI passes, there are no security issues and no unjustified force unwraps, the code follows patterns, and the description is adequate. **Request changes for:** security vulnerabilities, data-loss potential, breaking changes without migration, missing error handling. **⚠️ DO NOT MERGE.** The creating agent's monitor merges.

**After REQUEST_CHANGES (or APPROVE), report the verdict and stop.** Don't start a polling loop: when the author pushes fixes, `kb-pr-monitor` re-launches the gate with `--delta <sha>`, and that session re-reviews. First verify each requested change was made, then check the new fix code, skipping code already reviewed.

**Non-blocking suggestions become kanban subitems, not PR comments**, one per suggestion (within the finding budget):
`source {{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}/kanban-helpers.sh && kb-backlog sub add <ITEM-ID> "[Review] <actionable description> (PR #<N>)"`
Find the item ID from the launch prompt (`Kanban Item:`), else the branch name (`grep -oE '[A-Z]+-[0-9]+'`), else the PR body. Fall back to a PR comment only if none is found. These don't block the merge.

**Merge** (creating agent only, after all four gates): `gh pr merge <N> --squash --delete-branch --admin`. `--admin` is required because bot reviews don't count toward branch protection. Afterwards, verify `develop` builds and update the kanban.

